  "about": "I\u2019m Mila Arsenijevic, MSW RSW, founder and director of Toronto Therapy Practice (TTP) - a reproductive mental health hub that bridges clinical care, professional education, and corporate wellness.\n\nWith over a decade in Mount Sinai\u2019s Women & Infants Mental Health Program, I\u2019ve supported thousands of individuals and couples through fertility struggles, pregnancy, postpartum challenges, loss, and early parenting. Today, I lead a multidisciplinary team of senior therapists providing flexible, virtual therapy across Ontario and in-person support in Toronto.\n\nWhat sets me apart is the integration of therapy, training, and advocacy. Through my flagship course Therapy Essentials for the Reproductive Years, I train clinicians to confidently support clients through fertility, pregnancy, postpartum, and loss. I also partner with hospitals, fertility clinics, and corporations to deliver workshops that create systemic change in how we support family-building and parenthood at work.\n\nI believe mental health care should be both compassionate and practical, helping clients feel balanced and understood, while equipping professionals with tools they can apply immediately.\n\n\ud83d\udd39 Specialties: Fertility, pregnancy, postpartum, loss, couples therapy, workplace family-building support\n\ud83d\udd39 Services: Individual & couples therapy, clinical training, corporate workshops\n\ud83d\udd39 Vision: A world where reproductive and parental mental health are not an afterthought, but a cornerstone of well-being\n\nLet\u2019s connect if you\u2019re interested in:\n\u2714 Collaborating on mental health training or workshops\n\u2714 Bringing reproductive mental health expertise to your organization\n\u2714 Learning more about therapy or clinical education opportunities\n\u2026 more",
